WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:10.846
<v Priya>Good morning, everyone. Let’s do a quick status check on the dedupe fix and see where we stand for the Oct 29 launch.</v>

2
00:00:11.446 --> 00:00:14.523
<v Aisha>The dedupe-on-Plaid-transaction-ID fix is in review right now.</v>

3
00:00:15.123 --> 00:00:18.200
<v Jordan>Great, thanks. Anything else on the backend side?</v>

4
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:31.492
<v Aisha>I ran a dry-run backfill and discovered a new edge case: Capital One pending transactions change their ID when they post, so we need to match on amount, date and merchant as well.</v>

5
00:00:32.092 --> 00:00:37.862
<v Priya>Got it, so the logic needs to be broadened. How does that impact the timeline?</v>

6
00:00:38.462 --> 00:00:47.692
<v Aisha>I’ve adjusted the estimate and now expect the fix to land on October 19th, which is actually a day earlier than we originally planned.</v>

7
00:00:48.292 --> 00:00:54.446
<v Marcus>That’s good news for sales. We’ve already told 14 enterprise prospects about the Oct 29 date.</v>

8
00:00:55.046 --> 00:00:57.738
<v Priya>Excellent outreach, Marcus. Any feedback from them?</v>

9
00:00:58.338 --> 00:01:06.800
<v Marcus>Two of them asked for a demo the week of launch, so we’ll need to have the demo environment ready by then.</v>

10
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.631
<v Elena>I can prioritize the demo screens once the UI is locked.</v>

11
00:01:12.231 --> 00:01:17.615
<v Jordan>On the communications front, the weekly summary email template is drafted and looks solid.</v>

12
00:01:18.215 --> 00:01:21.677
<v Priya>What’s the metric we’re aiming for with that email?</v>

13
00:01:22.277 --> 00:01:26.508
<v Jordan>We’re targeting a 40 percent open rate for the first batch.</v>

14
00:01:27.108 --> 00:01:33.262
<v Aisha>The backfill for the dedupe fix is scheduled for the 21st, right after the code lands.</v>

15
00:01:33.862 --> 00:01:41.169
<v Priya>So the sequence is code merge on the 19th, backfill on the 21st, and we’ll be good to go?</v>

16
00:01:41.769 --> 00:01:44.846
<v Aisha>Exactly. Assuming the review passes without major comments.</v>

17
00:01:45.446 --> 00:01:50.446
<v Elena>I’ll make sure the support FAQ about duplicate transactions is ready by Friday.</v>

18
00:01:51.046 --> 00:01:54.123
<v Priya>Perfect, that ties into our launch communication plan.</v>

19
00:01:54.723 --> 00:02:00.877
<v Marcus>Just a reminder, the enterprise prospects will be expecting the FAQ link in the onboarding flow.</v>

20
00:02:01.477 --> 00:02:05.708
<v Jordan>Should we also note the FAQ in the weekly summary email?</v>

21
00:02:06.308 --> 00:02:09.769
<v Priya>Yes, let’s include a brief note with a link.</v>

22
00:02:10.369 --> 00:02:14.600
<v Elena>I can add that to the email copy before final approval.</v>

23
00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:23.662
<v Aisha>One more thing – the dedupe fix also handles Chase and Wells Fargo tokens after refresh, so we’re covering the previous bug.</v>

24
00:02:24.262 --> 00:02:26.762
<v Priya>Good, that clears the major blockers.</v>

25
00:02:27.362 --> 00:02:33.900
<v Marcus>No new feature requests should go into this sprint; we need to freeze everything except launch blockers.</v>

26
00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:38.346
<v Priya>Agreed, we’ll only merge items that are critical for launch.</v>

27
00:02:38.946 --> 00:02:43.946
<v Jordan>I’ll hold off on any enhancements to the categorizer until after Oct 29.</v>

28
00:02:44.546 --> 00:02:47.623
<v Elena>Same here, I’ll pause any non-essential design iterations.</v>

29
00:02:48.223 --> 00:02:54.377
<v Aisha>I’ll keep the review open for any urgent feedback but aim to merge by the 19th.</v>

30
00:02:54.977 --> 00:02:57.477
<v Priya>Anything else before we wrap up?</v>

31
00:02:58.077 --> 00:03:05.769
<v Marcus>Just to confirm, the demo environment will be ready by the 27th so we can run those two prospect demos.</v>

32
00:03:06.369 --> 00:03:23.677
<v Priya>Noted. Thanks, everyone. To recap: Aisha’s fix lands Oct 19, backfill on the 21st; weekly email drafted with a 40 % open target; we’re freezing new features; Elena will have the duplicate-transaction FAQ done by Friday. Let’s keep the momentum and hit the launch date.</v>
